Chief complaint: Cough and fever for five days, with shortness of breath on the stairs.

Diagnosis: Community-acquired pneumonia in the right lower lobe. The chest X-ray showed increased opacity in the same area. No signs of respiratory failure at the time of the visit.

Plan: Oral antibiotics for seven days, rest, and plenty of fluids. Follow-up in one week. Return sooner if the fever lasts longer than 72 hours.

